    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0668" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg546"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mutsu to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 11, 1889</date>.
                        (Received February 11.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just received the following telegram
                    from Count Okuma: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The constitution of the Empire was proclaimed by His Majesty in person
                            this morning amidst great enthusiasm of the people.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I hasten to communicate this important news, feeling assured that you will hear
                    it with interest, and that His Majesty the Emperor and the Government and people
                    of Japan will have, at this important epoch in the history of the Empire, the
                    best wishes of your Government and of the people of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Mutsu.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
